/*  Streams — `the input`, `the output`, `read a line from`, `read all from`, `read all lines from`,
    `Write … to <stream>`, and `With the file … open for reading as <name>: … Done.`

    ★ A stream is the C library's `FILE*`; `the input` is `stdin` and `the output` is `stdout`, as in
      `cufet build`.

    ★★ An open file is closed on EVERY way out of its block. Each one is registered with the
      runtime, which a caught exception's handler empties down to where its `Try` began — so a jump
      past the block closes it. Every other way out is known where it is written: `%files` lists the
      files open here, innermost last, and `%loop-files` and `%try-files` how many were open when
      the loop and the failure's `Try` around it began — the same bookkeeping `%rabbits` keeps.
*/

Pull books on collections, and the c-language.
    Bind fact to is-stream, given (the text kind):
        Return kind is "readable stream" or kind is "writable stream".
    Done.

    /// The kind a stream name of the language's own stands for, or "" for any other name.
    Bind text to standard-stream-kind, given (the text name):
        If name is "input", return "readable stream".
        If name is "output", return "writable stream".
        Return "".
    Done.

    Bind c-language axiom to standard-stream-c, given (the text name):
        If name is "input", return [stdin].
        Return [stdout].
    Done.

    /// The kind a read gives: a line — void at the end — everything, or every line.
    Bind text to stream-read-kind, given (the node expression):
        Define form as (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word.
        If form is "Line", return "voidable text".
        If form is "AllLines", return "series of text".
        Return "text".
    Done.

    /// A read as C.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-read unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define form as (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word.
        Define stream-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        If form is "All", return call-of-one on ("cufet_stream_read_all", stream-c).
        If form is "Line":
            Define c-language line-read, given (the c-language axiom held-stream),
                as [({ const char* cf_rl = cufet_stream_read_line(the held-stream); cf_rl ? cvo_text_some(cf_rl) : cvo_text_none(); })].
            Return line-read on (stream-c).
        Done.
        Define c-language lines-read, given (the c-language axiom held-stream),
            as [({ FILE* cf_rs = the held-stream; cser_text* cf_rln = cser_text_new(); const char* cf_ln; while ((cf_ln = cufet_stream_read_line(cf_rs)) != NULL) cser_text_append(cf_rln, cf_ln); cf_rln; })].
        Return lines-read on (stream-c).
    Done.

    /// `Write <text> to <stream>.` — as it is, no line's end added; flushed when it is the standard
    /// output, so a prompt shows before the read that waits for its answer.
    Bind void or failure to emit-stream-write unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        Define value-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Define stream-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Define c-language file-stream-fputs-form, given (the c-language axiom stream-c, the c-language axiom value-c),
            as [{ FILE* cf_ws = the stream-c; fputs(the value-c, cf_ws); if (cf_ws == stdout) fflush(cf_ws); }].
        Cast one's put on (file-stream-fputs-form on (stream-c, value-c)).
    Done.

    // ── Files open in a block ─────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// How many files are open here.
    Bind number to files-open unto emitter:
        Define open-names as the entry for "%files" in one's kinds but void is "".
        If open-names is "", return 0.
        Return the number of (open-names split by ",").
    Done.

    /// The C that closes the files opened since `depth`, innermost first — or "".
    Bind c-language axiom to c-leaving-files unto emitter, given (the text depth):
        Define open-names as the entry for "%files" in one's kinds but void is "".
        If open-names is "", return [].
        Define names as open-names split by ",".
        Define keep as depth converted to number but void is 0.
        Define c-language file-closed, given (the c-language axiom earlier, the term held-stream), as [the earlier cufet_close_file(the held-stream); ].
        Define out as cast no-c.
        Define place as the number of names.
        While place is greater than keep, repeat:
            The out becomes file-closed on (out, item place of names).
            Decrement place by 1.
        Done.
        Return out.
    Done.

    /// `With the file <path> open for reading as <name>: … Done.` — the file opened, its body run,
    /// and the file closed however the body is left.
    Bind void or failure to emit-with-open unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        Define reading as (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s word is "Reading".
        Define mode as "wb".
        Define stream-kind as "writable stream".
        If reading:
            The mode becomes "rb".
            The stream-kind becomes "readable stream".
        Done.
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
        Define stream-c as cast c-name on (name).
        Define path-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's put on ([{]).
        Define kept as cast one's kinds-kept.
        Define outer as one's indent.
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        Cast one's line on ("const char* cf_op = {path-c};").
        Cast one's line on ("FILE* {stream-c} = cufet_fopen(cf_op, \"{mode}\");").
        // Failing to open is a failure: to the `Try`'s handler, or — with none — said and stopped.
        Cast one's register-failable on ("failure of void").
        Define c-language file-opened, given (the term opened-c),
            as [({ cfl_void cf_w; memset(&cf_w, 0, sizeof cf_w); if (the opened-c) cf_w.ok = 1; else cf_w.failure = cufet_file_failure(cf_op, errno); cf_w; })].
        Define opened as file-opened on (stream-c).
        If cast one's current-try is not "":
            Cast one's line on ("{cast one's c-unwrapped on (opened, "failure of void")};").
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Define c-language cfl-opened-fpr-form, given (the c-language axiom opened),
                as [{ cfl_void cf_w = the opened; if (!cf_w.ok) { fprintf(stderr, "%s\n", cf_w.failure.message); exit(1); } }].
            Cast one's put on (cfl-opened-fpr-form on (opened)).
        Done.
        Cast one's line on ("cufet_reg_file({stream-c});").
        In one's kinds, the entry for name becomes stream-kind.
        Cast one's declared-here on (name).
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%{name}" becomes stream-kind.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "@{name}" becomes "".
        Define open-names as the entry for "%files" in one's kinds but void is "".
        If open-names is "", in one's kinds, the entry for "%files" becomes stream-c.
        Otherwise, in one's kinds, the entry for "%files" becomes "{open-names},{stream-c}".
        Define begun as cast one's opening-scope.
        For each inner in (cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s children, repeat:
            If cast declares-only on (inner) is false:
                Cast one's emit-statement on (inner) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
        Done.
        Cast one's closing-scope on (begun).
        Cast one's line on ("cufet_close_file({stream-c});").
        The one's indent becomes outer.
        The one's kinds becomes kept.
        Cast one's put on ([}]).
    Done.
Done.
